WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.030
- Fun in life.

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:06.680
If you don't have no fun in
life, ain't nothing happening.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.756
(metal creaking)

00:00:10.883 --> 00:00:12.410
- Hi Stephanie, I'm Avalon.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.450
Nice to meet you.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.260
- Hello, nice to meet you Avalon.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.260
- My name is Roland.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.250
- Good to meet you.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.640
- I'm 22 years old, it's
my last year in college.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.320
I'm just trying to figure
out what's next, I guess.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.370
- You're a senior in high school?

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.920
Do you know what your major is?

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.220
- Probably international affairs.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.870
- How did you go about choosing that?

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.100
- Well that's what I love.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.990
- You're at a point now where

00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:36.328
the world is your oyster.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.500
You must stay positive.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.613
It's your call.

00:00:39.613 --> 00:00:41.310
- I thought I wanted to be a nurse

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.290
because I wanted to help people.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.350
And I found out that it
was not good fit for me

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.490
and so, I wasted like
two years and some money.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.980
- I'm still learning so much about myself.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.300
There's so many things that I like,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.340
and so it's just like, it's
hard to narrow it down.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.370
- What do you like?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.690
- I love fashion.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.550
- Well you're dressed up
nice, I love your outfit.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:01.780
That jacket is on the move.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:02.613
- Thanks.

00:01:02.613 --> 00:01:04.850
- You could be excellent at that.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.310
Interviewing people about fashion.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:11.320
Keep your mind open,
create your own space.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.790
- In high school, I had
enjoyed taking my typing class

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.470
and I liked being organized.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.530
My friend suggested how about clerical,

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.590
how about going into secretarial?

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.688
So I went back to
college, changed my major,

00:01:21.688 --> 00:01:24.687
learned that, and I had many happy years

00:01:24.687 --> 00:01:26.750
as an administrative assistant.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.450
Also I advise young
people to talk to people

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.350
who know them really well,
whether it's a best friend,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.850
a boyfriend or girlfriend,
and they'll probably

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.970
have a very good insight.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.110
- I was the only black person
an all-white football team

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.210
and I was the quarterback and the captain.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.390
So I took that discipline
of all of that stuff with me

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.040
to UCLA and had a great time.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.930
But I made my own rules.

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.960
- And you can count all of
the black people at our school

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.310
and I was one of them
and it was just like,

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.640
and on top of me being like
gay and being openly gay

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.490
and androgynous, like, you
know, it was like definitely--

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:03.323
- It's a challenge.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.890
- It was a lot of
challenge but I liked it.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.940
- Intellectually,
spiritually, and passionately,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.520
you were above it all.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.080
That's how you were able to pull it off.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.430
- So love, I mean, I'm
about that age where

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.080
I should be starting to look
for my partner in crime.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.140
- I met my husband in college.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.060
I just liked so much about him.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.600
Of course, the big test
was to meet the family.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.400
- I'm the only girl in the family so

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:30.710
every single person's
gonna be so protective.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.800
- Very protective.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.400
- I feel bad for whoever I pick.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.293
Oh geez.

00:02:34.293 --> 00:02:35.820
- But I think when it's the right fit,

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.590
he'll fit right in and
they'll love him like a son.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.750
- They always say, like
you know, you, I guess,

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.890
like you want what you can't have.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.940
I guess that goes along
those lines because

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.910
I feel like I've through that too.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:50.270
But I was always after the
one that was just not really,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.560
I mean, that's just my experience.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.393
You know, I'm after the one--

00:02:52.393 --> 00:02:53.730
- You always want what you can't have.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.550
- Yeah, that was just like kind
of like, not texting me back

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.320
as much and just being like
whatever, you know, short

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.810
and because it was just
more of a, it was like more

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.643
intriguing.

00:03:02.643 --> 00:03:04.770
- That's always a learning experience.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.010
Why do I want that?

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.130
Why can't I get it?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.330
What's the best for me?

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.940
Sometimes you have to just let it slide.

00:03:14.429 --> 00:03:17.040
As my old grandmother
used to say, do without

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:18.660
and keep on moving.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:23.560
You know, I have just such
a broad spectrum of friends

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:27.160
and we're very open with one another.

00:03:28.009 --> 00:03:28.990
Be that way.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:30.630
Stay open.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.800
Keep the lines of communication open.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.370
Always make known your feelings

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.810
so there is no confusion.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:45.510
- Having raised four sons, we
never had a lot of extra cash.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.880
But we always look for
opportunities to have fun.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.260
Watching the sunrise over the mountain

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.550
or the sunset over the ocean.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.120
A kiss, a hug, a smile.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.910
There's a lot of beauty
to be found in life.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.010
And it doesn't cost a penny.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.450
The worst regrets that
I've heard is people saying

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:10.200
that they were too busy chasing success

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.970
or being selfish with their time.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.640
That they didn't spend time or
take time for their families.

00:04:18.021 --> 00:04:19.921
- You make me want to call my parents.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.273
- That's good.

